{"name":"Scooter","hex":"#308ea0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Scooter","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A male nickname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Scooter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kick scooter","blocks":[{"text":"A kick scooter is a human-powered street vehicle with a handlebar, deck, and wheels propelled by a rider pushing off the ground with their leg. Today the most common scooters are made of aluminum, titanium, and steel. Some kick scooters made for younger children have 3 to 4 wheels and are made of plastic and do not fold. High-performance kickbikes are also made. A company that had once made the Razor Scooters revitalized the design in the mid-nineties and early two-thousands. Three-wheel models whose frames fork into two decks are known as Y scooters or trikkes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Kickboards_Jahrhunderthalle_Probe_Zauberfl%C3%B6te_04-09-03.JPG/330px-Kickboards_Jahrhunderthalle_Probe_Zauberfl%C3%B6te_04-09-03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kick_scooter","wikidata":"Q502057"},{"title":"Eccentric-hub scooter","blocks":[{"text":"An eccentric-hub scooter is a two-wheeled human powered vehicle with an off centered hub on the large rear wheel. The scooter is powered by the rider making a bouncing motion on the platform."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eccentric-hub_scooter","wikidata":"Q5332175"},{"title":"Scooter (motorcycle)","blocks":[{"text":"A scooter or motor scooter is a motorcycle with an underbone or step-through frame, a seat, and a platform for the rider's feet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Yamaha_Aerox_2011_.jpg/330px-Yamaha_Aerox_2011_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scooter_(motorcycle)","wikidata":"Q193234"},{"title":"Scooter (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Scooter is a German happy hardcore, rave and techno music band founded in Hamburg in 1993. As of 2012, the band has sold over 30 million records and earned over 80 Gold and Platinum awards. Since December 2022, the band is composed of lead vocalist H. P. Baxxter, musician/producer Marc Blou, DJ/producer Jay Frog and manager Jens Thele."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Scooter_Chapter_7.jpg/330px-Scooter_Chapter_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scooter_(band)","wikidata":"Q156255"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/1936_avril_7_Lismonde_dessinant_%C3%A9glise_de_Diest_%28photo_L%C3%A9on_van_Dievoet%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-1936_avril_7_Lismonde_dessinant_%C3%A9glise_de_Diest_%28photo_L%C3%A9on_van_Dievoet%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/1936_avril_7_Lismonde_dessinant_%C3%A9glise_de_Diest_%28photo_L%C3%A9on_van_Dievoet%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-1936_avril_7_Lismonde_dessinant_%C3%A9glise_de_Diest_%28photo_L%C3%A9on_van_Dievoet%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/1936_avril_7_Lismonde_dessinant_%C3%A9glise_de_Diest_%28photo_L%C3%A9on_van_Dievoet%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-1936_avril_7_Lismonde_dessinant_%C3%A9glise_de_Diest_%28photo_L%C3%A9on_van_Dievoet%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An early kick scooter in Diest, Belgium, 1936. Photo by Léon van Dievoet.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1936_avril_7_Lismonde_dessinant_%C3%A9glise_de_Diest_(photo_L%C3%A9on_van_Dievoet)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Antique_sco